7. Summary
The study of logarithms is fundamental in both pure and applied mathematics. Understanding logarithms is essential for:

Simplifying complex multiplicative processes into additive ones.
Solving equations involving exponents.
Analyzing phenomena in science and engineering that exhibit exponential behavior.
Logarithms serve as a cornerstone in many quantitative aptitude problems, helping simplify analysis and improve problem-solving strategies in competitive environments.
